# Netlify headers — v30 (2026-11-06, owner order: speed up the site).
# Hashed assets (JS/CSS/fonts in /assets) are content-addressed: a new
# build gets a new filename, so the old file is never reused. Cache them
# immutably for a year — repeat visits load them from disk, not the
# network. HTML pages are NOT hashed, so they revalidate every time
# (visitors always see the latest version with a single ordinary refresh
# — the standing caching rule). Fonts and images are versioned by the
# build (they change rarely); cache them for a year but revalidate, so
# an updated file is picked up without a hard refresh.
# Note: Netlify already applies immutable caching to fingerprinted
# assets by default; these headers make it explicit and cover the
# fonts/img directories too.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, must-revalidate
/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, must-revalidate
/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
